Z||000009||ITB 2M4||12-22-2001||12:23 PM||||Just something else to add to your 'parts' thing....  While you have the front suspension apart, you might as well go with the MOOG 'Problem Solver' ball joints.  They might have had enough adjustment in them to get you the extra camber you needed.  But it will take some doing to get the old ball joints out, since they are pop riveted in.  Oh yeah, there are at least 3 different versions of the ball joint that I know of.  Be sure and get the one with the two cap screws for bolting to the upper control arm, and that the ball joint stud has a castle nut with a cotter pin.  This is the most heavy duty looking one, with a little bit of safety built in as well. <P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4<BR>AOL IM- DGPFiero||||reg||14
